Cell 5 – Generate a validation report
from pyspark.sql import functions as Fresults_df = spark.createDataFrame(RESULTS)display(results_df)results_df.createOrReplaceTempView(    "s3_presigned_validation_results")



You can now run a SQL query in another notebook cell:

%sql
SELECT
    timestamp_utc,
    scenario,
    status,
    hostname,
    detail
FROM s3_presigned_validation_results
ORDER BY timestamp_utc;



This provides the SQL-based evidence table for your S3 team.
4. Validate using Databricks SQL and Unity Catalog
If the S3 team also wants evidence of standard Databricks-to-S3 access, execute the following SQL using an approved external location.

-- Verify external location metadata
DESCRIBE EXTERNAL LOCATION
  `your_external_location`;

-- Validate SQL read access to an existing table
SELECT COUNT(*)
FROM your_catalog.your_schema.your_test_table;



A successful query confirms that the configured Databricks access path works. It does not establish that the SQL engine used a pre-signed URL.

For Serverless private connectivity, Databricks also documents validating access through an external location and SQL operations. 
